00/reb10/highres/5/E4513985_64.jpg"],"remarks":"There’s a particular quiet that comes with mature trees and a neighbourhood that’s had decades to settle in. In South Park, this 1976 two-storey comes with something newer communities can’t easily offer: a massive pie-shaped lot with a mature apple tree, fresh grass underfoot, and a deck made for long summer evenings around the firepit. Step inside, though, and the years fall away. Fresh flooring, paint and lighting lead to a kitchen with ceiling-height cabinetry and quartz counters. The primary has its own ensuite, and the bathrooms have been thoughtfully updated. The less glamorous work matters too: triple-pane windows, a new foundation membrane, weeping tile and sump pump. A tandem garage fits two vehicles, and the unfinished basement leaves room for whatever comes next. All the appeal of an established neighbourhood, without inheriting someone else’s renovation to-do list. (id:67522)","facts":[["Price","$459,900"],["Type","House"],["Bedrooms","3"],["Bathrooms","3"],["Half bathrooms","1"],["Living area","1,584 sq ft"],["Lot size","6,990 sq ft"],["Year built","1976"],["Storeys","2"],["Neighbourhood","South Park"],["Town","Leduc"],["Postal code","T9E4S7"],["MLS® number","E4513985"],["Listed","October 23, 2026"]],"features":[["Appliances","Washer, Refrigerator, Dishwasher, Stove, Dryer"],["Heating","Forced air"],["Basement","Unfinished, Full"],["Parking","Attached Garage"],["Community","Public Swimming Pool"]],"rooms":[["Living room","Main level","13'6 x 13'2\""],["Dining room","Main level","12'5 x 14'8\""],["Kitchen","Main level","12'5 x 12'9\""],["Primary Bedroom","Upper Level","12'6 x 13'11\""],["Bedroom 2","Upper Level","12'5 x 10'6\""],["Bedroom 3","Upper Level","9' x 12'2\""],["Breakfast","Main level","12'5 x 12'6\""]],"courtesy":"Ricky Aujla, Century 21 Bravo Realty and PJ Sangha, Century 21 Bravo Realty","board":"REALTORS® Association of Edmonton","town_slug":"leduc","hood_slug":"south-park","area":""}